    <title>Medications</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Medication</th><th>Frequency</th><th>Route</th><th>Dates</th><th>Status</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr ID="medication-1"><td>Naproxen 500 mg oral tablet twice daily, bought over the counter at full strength and taken most days for about two years for knee and back pain; stopped at intake</td><td>One tablet by mouth twice a day, self-directed</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1913-08-01 to 1915-08-04</td><td>stopped</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-2"><td>Losartan 50 mg oral tablet once daily</td><td>One tablet by mouth every morning</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1915-08-04 to 1915-09-15</td><td>completed</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-4"><td>Chlordiazepoxide 25 mg oral capsule, fixed five-day taper for alcohol withdrawal (four capsules on day 1, three on day 2, two on day 3, one on days 4 and 5), dispensed for five days only, with a daily telephone check</td><td>Up to one capsule four times a day on day 1, tapering to one a day by day 4; stop after day 5; no alcohol or driving</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1915-08-04 to 1915-08-08</td><td>completed</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-5"><td>Thiamine 100 mg oral tablet once daily</td><td>One tablet by mouth daily</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1915-08-04</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-6"><td>Acetaminophen 500 mg oral tablet, one or two tablets up to four times a day as needed for pain, no more than 2,000 mg in a day, in place of naproxen</td><td>One to two tablets by mouth every six hours as needed; no more than four tablets a day</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1915-08-04</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-7"><td>Naltrexone 50 mg oral tablet once daily, with a wallet card warning that it blocks opioid pain medicines</td><td>One tablet by mouth every morning</td><td>Oral route</td><td>1915-08-18</td><td>active</td><td>S</td></tr><tr ID="medication-10"><td>Diclofenac 1% gel, 4 g rubbed into the outer right ankle four times a day for up to seven days, in place of any oral anti-inflammatory medicine</td><td>Apply 4 g to the ankle four times a day for up to seven days</td><td>Topical route</td><td>1915-09-01 to 1915-09-08</td><td>completed</td><td>S</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

