    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Right ankle sprain (S93.401A)</content>. A moderate lateral ankle sprain. The Ottawa ankle rules are negative, so no X-ray is needed. [S]<list><item>Ice, compression and elevation for two to three days, a lace-up brace, and walking as pain allows, with ankle exercises from next week.</item><item>Acetaminophen up to 2,000 mg a day.</item><item>Diclofenac 1% gel to the ankle four times a day for up to seven days; no naproxen, ibuprofen or other anti-inflammatory tablets, which could harm his kidneys.</item><item>No opioid: naltrexone blocks it and an opioid would add risk in kidney disease and early recovery; if pain ever needs an opioid, it must be planned with this clinic.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder, severe, in early recovery (F10.20)</content>. One evening of drinking after 27 days, set off by pain: a lapse, not a return to daily drinking. He told it plainly and wants to go on. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; firearms still locked; 988 card carried. [S]<list><item>Continue naltrexone every morning.</item><item>Talk it through with the addiction counselor this week; a plan for pain and other triggers.</item><item>PEth at the six-week review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of Chronic Kidney Disease (2024); The American Psychiatric Association Practice Guideline for the Pharmacological Treatment of Patients With Alcohol Use Disorder (2018); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-week review in two weeks, or sooner for numbness, coldness of the foot, inability to bear weight, or any drinking he cannot stop. The clinic or 988 at any hour. Next scheduled visit 1915-09-15: six-week review: drinking and PEth, blood pressure, potassium and creatinine, urine albumin, liver tests, mood and safety. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
